{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I wish I were in London, Or some other seaport [D]town
[D]Set my foot in a steamboat And sail the ocean [G]round.
[G]While sailing on the ocean, While sailing on the [D]sea
[D]I'd think of handsome Molly Wherever she might [G]be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Remember Handsome Molly When you gave me your right hand?
And you said if you were to marry Then I'd be the man.
But now you broke your promise Go marry whom you please
While my poor heart is breaking You're going at your ease.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
She goes to church on Sunday And she passes me on by
I can tell her mind is changing By the roving of her eye.
Her hair is black as a raven Her eyes are black as a crow
Her cheeks look like linens out in the morning glow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I wish I were in London, Or some other seaport town
Set my foot in a steamboat And sail the ocean round.
While sailing on the ocean, While sailing on the sea
I'd think of handsome Molly Wherever she might be.
{end_of_verse}
